I can't speak to caveman, I don't remember any
details of my last game with one, but I played
knights-only for a very long stretch, to try to
figure out how they worked, as I'm doing now with
healers, and I can testify that a knight is just
plain discouraging to a beginner.

Knights are too soon burdened, their steed dies far
too easily, the knight "dies on the first attempt to
mount the steed" happens far too often, lots of
armor doesn't equal good armor, knight weapons suck
in unskilled hands, etc.

The advantages a knight has, like jumping as a great
technique for running away, just aren't accessible
to a beginner, who doesn't see how they are useful.

By the time the player is any good at the game,
being soured on knights has beecome a "way of life".

Thus, I'd say that your small sample is still a very
valid one for the ranking of the knight class, and I
suspect, but don't know on my own, that the same is
true for the caveman.

